User: The spherical tank of a water storage facility was 1/2 empty. When a pump was used in the capacity of a vacuum cleaner, it was able to pump out 8 gallons of water per minute. After the spherical tank was filled with this vacuum cleaner, it was 1/4 empty. How many gallons does it hold when it is full?
Assistant: <think> Let the capacity of the spherical tank be V gallons. Since the tank was 1/2 empty initially, it contained V/2 gallons. After pumping, it became 1/4 empty, meaning it contained 3V/4 gallons. The difference between 3V/4 and V/2 is the amount pumped out, which is 8 gallons per minute for the time taken to pump out 3V/4 - V/2 = V/4 gallons. The rate of pumping is 8 gallons per minute, so 8 tomatoes = V/4. Therefore, V = 32 gallons. </think> {{answer|32}}
<end>

